6. Save every profile variable to PNG
One figure per variable under plots/profile/. Existing files are skipped, so re-running is cheap; delete the directory to force a rebuild.


Code
profile_dir &lt;- file.path(plot_dir, "profile")
failed &lt;- list()
for (var in profile_vars) {
  out_path &lt;- file.path(profile_dir, paste0(var, ".png"))
  if (file.exists(out_path)) next
  p &lt;- tryCatch(plot_profile(var), error = function(e) e)
  if (inherits(p, "error")) {
    failed[[var]] &lt;- conditionMessage(p)
  } else {
    ggsave(out_path, p, width = 10, height = 4, dpi = 110)
  }
}
cat(sprintf("wrote %d profile PNGs to %s\n", length(profile_vars) - length(failed), profile_dir))
if (length(failed) &gt; 0) print(failed)

7. Save every zone variable to PNG
Zone variables are (nzones, time) — sediment fluxes and the sediment heat flux. sed_temp is handled separately in section 4 because it carries the extra sed_layers dimension.


Code
zone_dir &lt;- file.path(plot_dir, "zone")
failed_z &lt;- list()
for (var in zone_vars) {
  out_path &lt;- file.path(zone_dir, paste0(var, ".png"))
  if (file.exists(out_path)) next
  p &lt;- tryCatch(plot_zone(var), error = function(e) e)
  if (inherits(p, "error")) {
    failed_z[[var]] &lt;- conditionMessage(p)
  } else {
    ggsave(out_path, p, width = 10, height = 4, dpi = 110)
  }
}
cat(sprintf("wrote %d zone PNGs to %s\n", length(zone_vars) - length(failed_z), zone_dir))
if (length(failed_z) &gt; 0) print(failed_z)
